Hi Beno=EEt, Thara,

On Wed, 29 Sep 2010, Kevin Hilman wrote:

> Also, I'm still seeing this on boot:
>=20
>       omap_hwmod: sr1_fck: missing clockdomain for sr1_fck.
>       omap_hwmod: sr2_fck: missing clockdomain for sr2_fck.
>=20
> We need a final solution for this problem as a prerequisite for this
> series as well.

I guess we need to figure out the appropriate clockdomains for sr1_fck and=
=20
sr2_fck.

Probably the strictly correct thing to do, vis-a-vis the hardware, is to=20
place them into their own SmartReflex clockdomain/powerdomain.  But the=20
PRCM doesn't export separate control registers for those, and as I=20
understand it, that clockdomain/powerdomain follows the CORE=20
clockdomains/powerdomain.

Another option would be to place them into the WKUP clockdomain.  The=20
source of these functional clocks in SR_ALWON_FCLK which in turn is=20
generated by the PRM from SYS_CLK.  But that won't increment the CORE=20
clockdomains' use-counter when the SR functional clocks are running, which=
=20
seems desirable if the SmartReflex clockdomain/powerdomain really does=20
follow CORE.

So it seems to me that the best thing to do might be to place these clocks=
=20
into the CORE_L4 clockdomain.  But perhaps you might have a different=20
view?


regards,

- Paul
